{"id": "EUVD-2026-81784", "enisaUuid": "8407c66b-13c3-3ca1-81fb-2def0f861fed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmailbox: riscv-sbi-mpxy: validate RPMI notification lengths\n\nThe SBI return value controls how many bytes are copied from shared\nmemory into the RPMI notification buffer. It is not validated against\nthe negotiated shared-memory size before that copy. The event walker\nalso uses a reversed loop condition and can inspect a short event record.\n\nValidate the complete notification length before copying it, iterate only\nwhile a full event header remains, and stop when a declared event payload\nextends beyond the copied notification data.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:27", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbc24bce70dfd91c7b2f53b4fa896e9a4b6d6a6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c7bc5e7677bcda7a446d63b989cfaa3fe91d6b76", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11d5af151bcbe78f5a579e0faecd3be9cea0399a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m5w6-3p2w-2mgg", "CVE-2026-90191"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e75d727-431c-3c28-b055-64faab92eb27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf3022a4eb119c6b4e3424d6b19d8bfdfbc9bb57 <c7bc5e7677bcda7a446d63b989cfaa3fe91d6b76"}, {"id": "1cf0b47f-af05-32c4-87ce-d00811e9126a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "22c741f7-0f1e-30c1-9552-d299c47fd0c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "2fa81832-d132-33d8-9394-b7ee150381e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf3022a4eb119c6b4e3424d6b19d8bfdfbc9bb57 <11d5af151bcbe78f5a579e0faecd3be9cea0399a"}, {"id": "47303f38-efbb-3fc7-8488-f7925de0b156", 